      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Shaping the voice\n\nWorkflow 1 of three: **\"this is my voice, as I want it heard.\"** It ends in\nnode 9, which writes `sources/narration.wav` into a project folder — that file\nis what the reel graph reads, and nothing after this graph may re-time it.\n\n**Order matters.** Speed first, normalize last:\n`denoise → tempo → EQ → de-ess → compress → normalize`\nNormalizing before compression just gets undone by the compressor.\n\n## The knobs that change character\n\n| Node | Knob | What it changes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3 Pitch/Time | `pitch_semitones` | how high or low the voice sits |\n| 3 Pitch/Time | `tempo_factor` | how fast, pitch untouched |\n| 4 EQ | low / mid / high | weight, presence, air |\n| 6 Compressor | `ratio`, `threshold_db` | how even and how forward |\n\n## Recipes\n\n| Want | Change |\n|---|---|\n| **Deeper**, more authority | pitch `-1` to `-2`, EQ low `+2` @ `150` |\n| **Higher**, lighter | pitch `+1` to `+2`, EQ low `-3` @ `150` |\n| **Softer**, intimate | compressor ratio `2`, threshold `-24`, makeup `+6`; EQ high `-2`; de-ess ratio `4` |\n| **Punchier**, radio read | compressor ratio `5`, attack `3`, threshold `-22`, makeup `+6` |\n| **Brighter**, crisper | EQ mid `+2` @ `3000`, high `+3` @ `6000` |\n| **Warmer**, rounder | EQ low `+2` @ `200`, high `-2` @ `8000` |\n| **Faster** for reels | tempo `1.15` |\n| **Telephone / walkie** | EQ low `-12` @ `300`, high `-12` @ `3000` |\n\nChange one thing at a time. To audition without writing the file, drop a\n**Preview Audio** node on the node 7 output and bypass node 9 (ctrl+B).\n\n## Pitch in plain terms\n\n`pitch_semitones` is musical steps, accurate to a hundredth of a step.\n`-1` is subtle, `-2` reads as a different person, `-3` starts to sound\nprocessed. Past `+/-4` speech turns artificial.\n\nPitch and tempo are **independent**, and formants are preserved, so\nspeeding up does *not* make it chipmunky. Leave pitch at `0` unless you\nactually want a different voice.\n\n## EQ gotcha\n\n`low_freq` and `high_freq` are **shelf corners**: you get *half* the dB you\ndialled at that exact frequency, and the full amount about an octave past it.\nMeasured on the current setting (low `-4` @ `110`, high `+2` @ `7000`):\n\n`60 Hz -3.7` · `110 Hz -2.0` · `200 Hz -0.3` · `7000 Hz +1.2` · `12k +2.0`\n\nSo to actually cut 4 dB of rumble *at* 110 Hz, set the corner near `220`.\n`mid` is a bell, not a shelf: full gain right at `mid_freq`. Widen with\n`mid_q` below `1`, narrow above.\n\n## Levels\n\nNode 7 sets the ceiling, `-1.0 dBFS` — the headroom the one AAC encode at the\nend of the reel needs. Node 8 reads what you actually made: Instagram and\nTikTok normalise to about `-14 LUFS`, so land near it and the platform leaves\nthe reel alone.\n\nAs it stands this chain measures **-13.4 LUFS** (20 s of the\nlegends_of_surrender voiceover, 2026-09-03) - it was `-15.3` when the\nceiling was `-2.0`. A decibel of ceiling is roughly a decibel of loudness,\nand compressor `makeup_gain_db` is the other handle.\n\n## Denoise (node 2) is ON\n\n`spectral_gate` at `0.5` thins steady hiss with a soft spectral mask and\nleaves room tone alone. `noise_gate` is the blunt version for bad takes.\n`strength 0.0` is passthrough. Turn it off (ctrl+B) if the source is clean —\nany denoiser costs a little detail.\n\n## Auto-Tune\n\n**MemoActs — Auto-Tune** is in the same menu and is not in this chain: it\npulls drifting pitch toward a scale, which a spoken read rarely wants. It is\ngentle by construction — the stretcher follows a curve to about 1–2 Hz and\nspeech moves at 4–8 Hz, so `retune_ms` floors at 150 and a hard snap is not\non offer.\n\n## Node 9 — into the project\n\nType a folder name. A name nobody has used is **made** into an empty project;\nan existing one is used as it stands. The node writes 24-bit PCM at the\nincoming rate, moves any competing `narration.*` to `archive/`, and skips the\nwrite when the samples already match — so re-queuing this graph does not touch\nthe mtime the alignment cache is keyed on.\n\n---\n\nNodes: `memoacts/audio` in the node menu, from this pack\n(`custom_nodes/MemoActStudio`). They need `pedalboard` and `pyloudnorm`;\n`pip install -r requirements.txt` into the embedded Python covers both.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "MemoActs - voiceover: speed up + normalize + filters\n\nREQUIRED CUSTOM NODE PACK:\n  custom_nodes/memoacts_audio  (local, in this repo)\n    -> AudioPitchTime, AudioNormalize, AudioVocalCompressor,\n       AudioDeEsser, AudioSpeechDenoise, AudioLoudnessMeter\n  core ComfyUI\n    -> LoadAudio, AudioEqualizer3Band, PreviewAudio, SaveAudioAdvanced\n\n  The pack is backed by pedalboard (Rubber Band time-stretch + JUCE DSP),\n  scipy and pyloudnorm. All three ship with this ComfyUI env already,\n  so there is nothing to pip install. Restart ComfyUI after pulling.\n\nORDER MATTERS. Speed first, normalize last:\n  denoise -> tempo -> EQ -> de-ess -> compress -> normalize\n  Normalizing before compression gets undone by the compressor.\n\nSPEED: node 3, tempo_factor.\n  1.10 = light, 1.15 = the usual reels lift, 1.25 = audible.\n  Above ~1.3 Russian narration starts to sound rushed. Range 0.5-2.0.\n  Keep pitch_semitones at 0 -- tempo and pitch are independent here,\n  and formants are preserved, so the voice does not turn chipmunky.\n\nDENOISE (node 2) is BYPASSED (ctrl+B toggles).\n  method=spectral_gate is a soft Wiener mask over an estimated noise\n  floor: it thins steady hiss and hum but leaves room tone alone.\n  method=noise_gate is a hard downward gate for worse recordings.\n  strength 0.0 = passthrough, 1.0 = aggressive.\n\nOPTIONAL: drop an AudioLoudnessMeter on the node 7 output and route its\nreport STRING to a Preview Any / ShowText node. It reports integrated\nLUFS + peak. Instagram targets about -14 LUFS; this chain lands near\n-13.4 LUFS on the legends_of_surrender voiceover at tempo 1.15.\n\nPIPELINE NOTE: this runs BEFORE the reel render. The sped-up file becomes\nthe new narration.mp3 master clock. The renderer itself never time-stretches\naudio (Reel Renderer Spec v1, Stage 6)."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "title": "How to shape the voice"
